0..75 Comment "// A program decides two bounds on `e`: `1000 · exp 1` lies between `2718`"
76..152 Comment "// and `2719`. It works through `std.reals.Eff`, the host interface of exact"
153..162 Comment "// reals."
163..165 Comment "//"
166..236 Comment "// No plan of field operations and cuts defines `e`. A recurrence node"
237..314 Comment "// defines it: the sum of a series whose term ratio is a rational function of"
315..393 Comment "// the index. The plan of `exp 1` is the series of ratio `1 / (n + 1)` at one,"
394..430 Comment "// and `exp` has no rule of its own."
431..433 Comment "//"
434..505 Comment "// The host encloses the series by a partial sum and a tail bound, at a"
506..578 Comment "// precision that doubles. The checker replays each step before the host"
579..651 Comment "// replies. `gandr run exponential.gandr` prints `holds holds`. The same"
652..723 Comment "// `decided` runs under a handler of this source, a second model of the"
724..737 Comment "// interface."
738..740 Comment "//"
741..816 Comment "// - see: `crates/theory-exact-reals/src/recurrence.rs` — the rule of the"
817..837 Comment "//   recurrence node"
838..914 Comment "// - see: `corpus/model/reals/trigonometry.gandr` — the builtins of a plan"
916..948 Comment "// The console\'s host interface."
